      "content": "thanks. that's a good start. but looking at the wording for the second part... calling it a \"potential loss of cultural exchange\" sounds a bit like we're downplaying the actual ownership issues. if we're being realistic for this document, which side has the more ethically sound argument when it comes to correcting historical wrongs? like, shouldn't the moral imperative to right colonial-era seizures take precedence over just \"accessibility\"?",
