      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The universal museum argument is fundamentally flawed and perpetuates a form of cultural imperialism. The idea that certain treasures belong to all of humanity is a convenient excuse for Western institutions to hoard artifacts from other countries. The moral imperative of repatriation is not just about correcting historical wrongs; it's about acknowledging the sovereignty and cultural identity of nations. The scientific and educational value of these collections is irrelevant when weighed against the right of a people to their own heritage. It's time for universal museums to stop acting as colonial relics and start returning artifacts to their rightful owners.",
